Chapter: PunctualHeapConstruction

 Punctual functions that heap-allocate through construction rather
 than a named builtin: a record literal and a list literal. Both go
 through the R10 bump allocator and must be rejected with CDX6002;
 an earlier checker flagged only allocating builtins and text
 concatenation, so both of these compiled clean.

Section: Definitions

  Point = record {
   px : Integer,
   py : Integer
  }

  punctual bad-make-point : Integer, Integer -> Point
  bad-make-point (a) (b) = Point { px = a, py = b }

  punctual bad-make-list : Integer -> List Integer
  bad-make-list (n) = [n, n]

  opening : Integer = 0
